1	/*
2	 * boot_clock.c - BK7258 cold-start DPLL enable (product-grade).
3	 *
4	 * On cold reset the BootROM leaves EN_DPLL=0.  This module mirrors the
5	 * Armino SDK sys_hal_early_init analog-register sequence to enable and
6	 * calibrate the DPLL before jumping to the app, so the app can
7	 * deterministically switch the core mux to 320 MHz on both cold and soft
8	 * reset paths.
9	 *
10	 * Board chip_id = 0x23A40910 = PM_CHIP_ID_MP_C.  The SDK has no explicit
11	 * MP_C branch, so the default else-branch ANA_REG values apply
12	 * (sys_hal.c:2865-2876).
13	 *
14	 * Product-grade safety:
15	 *   - Skip the full sequence if EN_DPLL is already set (soft-reset path
16	 *     where the loader already enabled DPLL).
17	 *   - Every analog-SPI write has a bounded timeout (ANA_SPI_TIMEOUT); if
18	 *     any write times out, the remaining sequence is aborted and control
19	 *     returns to the caller.  The app's 26 MHz fallback handles the case
20	 *     where the DPLL ends up not enabled.
21	 *   - No step can hang the bootloader indefinitely.
22	 *
23	 * Scope: DPLL enable + SPI recalibration only.  Does NOT switch the core
24	 * mux (M1) or the flash clock (M2 cksel_flash) -- switching flash to the
25	 * 480 MHz source stalls on this board; the core mux is left for the app.
26	 *
27	 * Freestanding: no libc, no .data/.bss globals, only stack locals.
28	 */
29	
